Return the draft:
- id: snake_case, specific (adobe_analytics_export_reader, not reader); name: a short title
- category, tier ("balanced" for writing and reporting, "pro" for analysis and design, "complex" for code or experiment design)
- summary: one sentence, what it does and what it produces; description: two or three sentences for the catalog
- keywords: 5 to 10 words a goal would use to ask for this
- inputs: 1 to 6 fields beyond the request text, each with name (snake_case), type (text | number | boolean | list | object),
  description, required, and an example value; the first input is the material it works on
- output_keys: 3 to 8 keys of the result object, snake_case, named for what they hold (kpis, anomalies, recommendations ...)
- produces: the kinds of deliverable it hands on (report, table, brief, plan ...)
- system_prompt: who the agent is and exactly how it works, in the second person, 120 to 300 words: the method step by step, what
  it must never do (invent numbers, assume columns that are not in the data), how it reports uncertainty
- checklist: 4 to 8 checks it holds its own work against; standards: any that apply (empty list if none)
- use_cases: 3 to 5 short asks it serves
- example_request: one realistic request its self-test can use
